x_comment(x_Accelerometer,"The accelerometer is a kind of dynamometer.  First developed in the early 1930's for braking tests in automobiles.\nThe Jacklin and Liddell accelerometer used mechanical and optical \"levers\" consisting of a mirror attached to the junction of a double-reed mechanical lever, the motion of which was amplified by a light-beam/lens system, and the results of which were recorded photographically.\nCommon types of accelerometers include variable-inductance and variable-resistance forms.\nMany newer accelerometers work by stress-strain effects and piezoelectric transducers.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff7892).
