x_comment(x_AcetelyneRediscovered,"Bertholot rediscovered and named acetelyne.\nIt had previously been prepared by John Davy in 1836 (cf Partington, p.232), and in 1862 was prepared from calcium carbide by Woler (specifically by heating an alloy of zinc and calcium with carbon) (cf, Partington p. 238, 351).  In 1864, Kekule obtained acetelyne by the electrolysis of fumaric acid (Partington p.294)\nAcetelyne is especially important in welding.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff789e).
