x_comment(x_AckermannsSteeringGear,"A kinematic linkage that allows a vehicle to steer by turning the inner wheel more tightly than the outer wheel.  The two wheels are kept tangential to the common center of the turn, but are not parallel to each other.\nThis follows from the tie rod being shorter than the axle.\nPatented by Ackermann, but invented previously by Du Quet for windmill carraiges (1714) and Lankensperger for horse-drawn carraiges (1816)") :- x_cid(a65b125fff78b8).
