x_comment('x_Barkhausen-KurzOscillator',"An ultra-high frequency (for the time) oscillator that was a forerunner to the microwave tube.  This was the first tube capable of working at centimeter wavelengths.  It was a triode tube with a positive grid and the anode slightly negative with respect to the cathode, such that electrons accelerated towards the grid, mostly missed and were repelled back by the anode in rapid oscillation.  Attained high frequency at the expense of low power.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff7bb3).
