x_comment('x_BorosilicateGlass-Pyrex',"Typically used for oven and lab-ware, borosilicate glass is made by replacing much of the soda ash in the recipe with boric oxide.  Borosilicate glass has a much lower coeficient of thermal expansion than soda glass and can be cooled by 200 degress Celsius without danger of cracking.\nBecause it has a low coefficient of thermal expansion, Pyrex replaced regular glass in telescope mirrors between WWI and WWII, after which it was replaced by quartz.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff7cf0).
