x_comment(x_Coherer,"Marconi's first detector.  A heap of metal filings between two metal rods enclosed in a glass tube. When an electric wave passes, the filings \"cohere\" and become conducting.  The closed circuit rings a bell or taps the coherer and shakes up the filings so they once again conduct poorly.  (Crowther, p. 351)\nThe name \"coherer\" was bestowed by Sir Oliver Lodge in his memorial lecture on Hertz, in 1894 (cf, Dunsheath, 1968)\nReplaced in 1901 by the magnetic detector, and later, the crystal detector.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff80af).
