x_comment(x_CombustionChamberForJetEngine,"The combustion chamber for the first Whittle jet engine needed to raise the temperature of air leaving the compressor from 204degC to 788degC where it entered the turbine.  It needed to burn kerosene as completely as possible in the smallest space with minimal drop in pressure.\nHawthorne showed that at sufficiently high speed (ie, with turbulence), the turbulent mixing rate dominates the rate of combustion.  Ie, aerodynamic rather than chemical processes are dominant.\nSolved the problem by carefully atomizing the liquid spray injection.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff80f7).
