x_comment('x_CoolidgeX-rayTube',"The model on which all medical X-ray tubes are based.\nIn 1913, Coolidge introduced the x-ray tube with high vacuum.  In 1916, he replaced the cold aluminum cathode with a hot tungsten cathode. (cf, Crump, p.194)\nAn alternative to the earlier, short-lived gas-discharge tubes, it accelerates electrons toward a water-cooled tungsten anode where 1% of the beam energy is turned into x-rays and the rest into heat.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff821f).
