x_comment('x_Copper-to-GlassSeal',"Copper has a much larger coefficient of thermal expansion than glass.  Electrodes are hammered flat so the copper's ductility compensates for thermal expansion.\nThis is effectively a geometric strategy because it maximizes surface area.\nAlso known as the \"Housekeeper Seal\"\nsee: \"The art of sealing base metals through glasss' by W.G. Housekeeper.  J. Am. IEE col 41, p. 870, 1923.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8230).
