x_comment('x_Double-dopingTechnique',"The Bell-Labs method of producing junction transistors of sufficiently narrow thickness.  Involved adding small pellet of impurity to the surface of the melt during the crystal growing process, stirring the melt to ensure uniform doping, removing the pellet for a short period to grow the base region, then re-introducing dopant (hence \"double-doping\")\nIn 1951, Sparks grew NPN transistors with p-layers 1-2 mils thick.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff84a5).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fff84a5,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
