x_comment(x_ElectrokineticPhenomena,"Electro-osmosis (electroendosmosis) is the movemen of a polar fluid or an electrolyte by an electric current through a porous diaphragm.  Convesely, the movement of a liquid through a porous diaphragm induces a voltage (streaming potential) across the diaphragm to the pressure difference.\n(the porous diaphragm is a small capillary)\nCataphoresis involves suspended colloids move in a direction reverse to that of the fluid. (only for low voltages)\nIn some cases, particles settling can produce an emf.\nUsed in flow meters and transducers\ncf Ganot's physics.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8665).
