x_comment(x_EniacElectronicDigitalComputer,"Eniac was the first general purpose electronic digital computer, though not a stored program machine.  It was an order of magnitude faster than the Harvard Mark I.\nDeveloped at the University of Pennsylvania.  Installed at Aberdeen Proving Ground, Maryland.  Used 18,000 vacuum tubes (hence the classification  \"new principle\" as an improvement on electromechanical relays)\nBecause ENIAC worked with decimal numbers rather than straight binary, it was more complex by an order of magnitude than it needed to be.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff874f).
