x_comment(x_FirstV2RocketPrototypeIsLaunched,"First large-scale liquid fuel rocket for military purposes.\nThe German development program started in 1940, and the first V2 was launched July 6, 1942.  The third prototype, launched October 1942, was the first successful flight, flying 170 miles.\nBurned alcohol and liquid oxygen.  Used glass wool insulation around LOX tanks.\nLaunch process: alcohol & LOX fed by gravity to combustion chamber, where they ignite on contact, producing 16,000 lbs of thrust.  Propellant turbine then activated, increasing thrust to 52,000lbs, launching rocket.  68 second burn time.\nLaunch weight = 28,413 lbs, including 19,575 lbs fuel.\nStabilizing fins included steering vanes with vane motors and antennas.\nTurbopump driven by steam generated from hydrogen peroxide + sodium permanganate, fed by compressed air.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8a21).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fff8a21,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
