x_comment(x_FizeausWaterDragExperiment,"An important early attempt to detect the motion of the aether.  It showed that the velocity of light increases in a medium according to the formula v (1- 1/n^2), where v = velocity of the medium and n = its refractive index.\n\"His apparatus consisted of parallel tubes through which he sent water at high speeds in opposite directions.  He split a single beam of light into two fractions, and with a mirror he made each traverse the tubes in opposite directions.  He then compared the interference fringes produced by light moving with and atgainst the fcurrent and found them displaced in opposite senses by measurable and reproducible amounts.\"  \n(Gillispie, The Edge of Objectivity, p.427)\nPublished in 1859 in Annales de chimie et de physique.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8a28).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fff8a28,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
xc_source_file(a65b125fff8a28,'c:/snet/petta/repos/openworld_dr/KBs/companions/v1/flat-files/tech-kb/innovations.krf').
