x_comment('x_High-intensityPulsedMagneticFields',"Kapitza achieved high magnetic fields by switching the current from a dedicated generatator as it crossed 0 volts and switching it off when it again reached 0 volts.  He minimized the disruption to the measurements from  the mechanical shock when the generator suddenly halts due to the enourmous load, by placing the generator at the other end of the building, so the transmission delay exceeded the measurement duration.  A similar strategy was later used in the Teller-Ulam device.\nKapitza, P.L., Proc Royal Soc. A v.115, pp 658-683, 1927") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8ed0).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fff8ed0,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
