x_comment(x_HunningsTransmitter,"British patent received 1878 for a loose carbon granule telephone transmitter, in which \"engine coke\" is contained between an electrically conducting diaphragm of platinum, silver, ferrotype or tinned iron and a brass disk.  Increased surface area contact enabled higher currents and series resistance, thereby modulating higher power with about 9dB increase in efficiency over the Berliner, Edison and Blake transmitters.\nRefined by American Bell Co. in 1885 to use a horizontal diaphragm, hard carbon granules and gold-plated electrodes. To become the \"long-distance\" transmiter.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8f5f).
