x_comment(x_HydraulicForgingPress,"A force amplifier relying on incompressibility of liquids.\nAt one end is a small area piston driven by a lever to increase mechanical advantage.  Small diameter tubing leads to the other end of the system , where a large diameter piston exerts a large force equal to the force exerted on the small piston multiplied by the ratio of the areas.\nFox developed a cropping and shearing press (possibly at the suggestion of Naysmith) that he applied to producing chain links made of flat bar for use in suspension bridges.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8f8a).
