x_comment(x_HydraulicReactionTurbine,"Achieved 80% improvement in turbines by eliminating sharp bends in fluid flow.  Essentially a water wheel on its side.  The critical difference between a water wheel and a turbine is that the turbine is driven by the kinetic energy of the flowing water, not the weight.\nThe Fourneyron turbine in particular was a reaction turbine, as opposed to impulse.  It achieved effiency by reducing exit velocity with precisely curved blades, and minimizing entry shock via carefully controlled angle of entry.  The Fourneyron turbine was an outward-flow turbine, which was largely superceded by inward-flow configurations.\nImproved reaction turbines have achieved up to 50,000 horsepower.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff8fa9).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fff8fa9,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
