x_comment('x_KerrElectro-OpticEffect',"The rotation of the plane of polarisation of light in passing through an optical medium across which an electric potential is applied.\nWhen an optically isotropic substance is placed in a strong electric field, it becomes doubly refracting.\nThe effect is proportional to the square of the applied field.\nSee also Cotton-Mouton Effect and Pockels Effect.\nThis is one of the first nonlinear optical effects,  currently finding application in laser transmission.\nKerr, J. Phil. Mag. 1875, 50 , 337; 446") :- x_cid(a65b125fff92af).
