x_comment(x_KiwiNuclearReactor,"The Kiwi reactor was developed by the AEC and NASA to power the NERVA nuclear rocket.  Developed between ~1956-1966.  The Kiwi was approximately 12 feet long and generated 1,000 megawatts of power.  It saved weight by replacing control rods with rollers around the core whose surface was coated with boron on one side and beryllium on the other. In one position, the boron would absorb neutrons.  When rotated, the beryllium would reflect reflect neutrons back into the core to increase fission.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff92e8).
