x_comment(x_KondoEffect,"An anomalous resistance minimum in dilute magnetic alloys.  The resistivity of these alloys decreases with temperature, then begins to rise as temperature continues to decrease down to that of liquid helium.\nFirst observed by Meissner in 1930, and explained in Jun Kondo's paper \"Resistance Minimum in Dilute Magnetic Allows\", published in Progress of Theoretical Physics, v.32(1964) 37.\nMore recently, the Kondo Effect has become relevant in the study of quantum dots.  C.f., Science May 28, 2004, p.1293 \"Photon-Induced Kondo Satellites in a Single-Electron Transistor.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff92ff).
