x_comment(x_LawOfTheInclinedPlane,"The force acting down an inclined plane due to weight W is W sin alpha, where alpha is the angle of inclination.\nProved by a thought experiment consisting of a heavy frictionless loop of rope draped over a (non-equilateral) triangular prism.  The forces on the rope segments must balance, else there would be perpetual motion, so the different weights of the segments must be balanced by the sins of the angles.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff93df).
