x_comment(x_MaupertuisPrincipleOfLeastAction,"A crude mathematical attempt to capture the notion of a \"minimum quantity of action\".\n\"[He] takes the \"action\" of a moving body as the integral of the momentum with respect to distance along the path and asserts that nature wishes to economize as much as possible in dispensing this quantity.\" - Truesdell p.132\nThis was an attempt to generalize Fermat's Principle of Least Time and Snell's law in optics.  Euler gave a more correct but less general formulation in 1843.  Further refinement was due to Lagrange, Hamilton and Jacobi.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff9739).
