x_comment('x_PolaroidJ-Sheet',"Kind of at the boundary between stuff, process, and device.  The J-sheet was an inexpensive means of producing polarizing filters.  Land made herapathite in submicroscopic particles, mixed into a plastic mass, oriented them within the plastic while forming a finished transparent sheet.  This was an alternative to trying to construct single large crystals.\nPerpendicular polarizers block light transmission in a manner Land thought of as a kind of light valve.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff9ea4).
