x_comment(x_ProcessForMakingTungstenDuctile,"Enabled use of tungsten in continuous filament light bulbs.\nG.E. bought german patents and introduced tungsten filaments in 1907.  They were 100% more efficient than tantalum but extremely fragile.  Coolidge developed the method for producing ductile tungsten by sintering, hot swaging, then repeatedly drawing the filament through progressively smaller heated dies.  Unlike other metals, tungsten becomes more ductile the more it is worked at hight temperature.  When ductile, it has fibrous structure, whereas it is crystalline when brittle.") :- x_cid(a65b125fff9fcb).
