x_comment(x_ProximityFuze,"Problems addressed by the proximity fuze include:\nruggedization, miniaturization, long-shelf-life power supply, safety, radio detection, waterproofing, etc.\nIts development depended on electronics (thyratron, amplifier, transmitter/retriever), plastics (nose cone had to be transparent to radio), packaging (4 vacuum tubes potted in rubber, whole package encapsulated in monocrystalline wax via pressure cooker), mechanical safety devices activated from shell spin @400rps and launch acceleration @20,000Gs)\nUsed a custom-made cylindrical capacitor of vinyl carbazole-treated cellophane dielectric film to provide the charge for detonation.\n\"reserve cell\" batteries kept electrolyte isolated in glass ampules from zinc & carbon plates.  On firing, the ampules broke and the electrolyte was distributed uniformly over the plates by the spinning of the shell.  Activated in 0.1s for 2-min duration flight.  Supplied 1.5V, 97V & 7.5V.") :- x_cid(a65b125fffa03e).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fffa03e,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
