x_comment(x_RootsBlower,"A positive-displacement compressor consisting of two or more figure-eight shaped lobes driven by gears to mesh closely without actually touching.  The absence of contact permits operation without lubricants but limits the attainable pressure differential.\nIt supplies higher pressure than the centrifugal fan.\nFirst invented by Isaiah Davies in 1848, it was applied by the Roots brothers as a water wheel in their woolen mill.\nToday it is more commonly employed in automotive superchargers and vacuum pumps.") :- x_cid(a65b125fffa305).
