x_comment(x_RuhmkorffCoil,"An adjustable, high voltage source (typically a few kilovolts), that substituted for batteries in high voltage applications.  The rhumkorff coil preceded the AC transformer.\nThe induction coil worked similarly to an electric buzzer + a transformer, in that the primary coil was connected in series with a leaf switch that broke contact whenever the coil was energized.\nRuhmkorff perfected the induction coil by more carefully insulating the wires from each other, from the core, and adding paper insulation between the coils.  He also radically scaled up the number of turns in the secondary coil.  Unlike a transformer, the coils are concentric.") :- x_cid(a65b125fffa34e).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fffa34e,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
