x_comment(x_StokesLaw,"Describes the force needed to keep a small sphere moving at uniform speed through a fluid.\nIt entails 5 assumptions (cf, Millikan, p. 93):\n1) inhomogeneities in the medium are small compared to the size of the sphere,\n2) the sphere falls as it would in a medium of indefinite extent,\n3) the sphere is smooth and rigid,\n4) there is no slippage of the medium over the surface of the sphere, and\n5) the velocity of the sphere is sufficiently small that the resistance to motion is entirely due to viscosity of the medium and not to inertia of the portion of medium being pushed forward.") :- x_cid(a65b125fffa778).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fffa778,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
