x_comment(x_SuperheterodyneRadioCircuit,"The basic circuit behind AM radio.  Separates out selection and tuning from amplification in order to minimize oscillation. Output from a low-or-no gain bandpass filter is mixed with a local oscillator to produce a fixed intermediate frequency signal (~455KHz) between the radio freq and audio frequencies.  A stable bandpass filter/amplifier amplifies this signal, to which envelope detection is applied and the resulting audio signal is amplified at the output stage.") :- x_cid(a65b125fffa817).
