x_comment('x_Teller-UlamDevice',"The hydrogen bomb trigger is the classic example of overcoming a barrier to process initiation.  The problem was how to initiate fusion before the bomb blew itself apart.  The key idea was that the radiation pressure from a fission bomb would outrace the mechanical shockwave.  Thus the core strategy is a race between two processes, rather than a bootstrap of progressively more powerful triggers (which it also was).") :- x_cid(a65b125fffa8f0).
