x_comment(x_ThirdLawOfThermodynamics,"The entropy change in a reaction between pure substances approaches zero at T = 0 K.\nMax Planck subsequently (1912) made the stronger statement: \"As the temperature diminishes indefinitely, the entropy of a chemically homogeneous body of finite density approaches indefinitely near to the value zero\" (M. Planck, Treatise on Thermodynamics).\nAs a consequence, it follows from the Third Law that the absolute zero of the (absolute) temperature scale, i.e., a temperature of zero kelvin (T = 0 K) cannot be attained by any means.") :- x_cid(a65b125fffaa18).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fffaa18,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
