x_comment(x_TransmissionLineTheory,"The increased frequencies of telephone transmission required better analysis of the role of impedance.\nHeaviside's eqns:\n(1) A ~ R (sqrt C/L + G (sqrt (L/C)\nwhere \nA = attenuation (in dB/unit length)\nR = series resistance\nL = series inductance\nC = shunt capacitance\nG = shunt conductance\nAt telegraph frequencies (~10 Hz), this is almost completely resistive\nFor multiwire telegraph cable, (with higher C and lower L), attenuation is 10 - 25 times higher and can be approximated by:\n(2) A ~ (sqrt (RCf)\nwhere f is the frequency\n(c.f. Physics in the communications industry)") :- x_cid(a65b125fffaac3).
xc_microtheory(a65b125fffaac3,x_MetaengineeringInnovationsMt).
