x_comment(x_Turbine,"An engine with only one moving part, capable of continuous motion.\nAlternative to reciprocal or piston engines.\nDriven by impulse and/or reaction forces.\nThe difference between a water-mill and a water turbine is that a mill is driven primarily by the weight of the water, not the kinetic energy.\nThe term \"turbine\" was coined by Claude Burdin.") :- x_cid(a65b125fffab82).
